text Errors involving limits that have been imposed merely to simplify the language
text Some conformance errors simplify the language that authors need to learn.
text For example, the  element's  attribute, despite accepting both  and  values in practice as synonyms, disallows the use of the  value, so as to simplify tutorials and other learning aids. There would be no benefit to allowing both, but it would cause extra confusion when teaching the language.
