text Certain elements are parsed in somewhat eccentric ways (typically for historical reasons), and their content model restrictions are intended to avoid exposing the author to these issues.
text For example, a  element isn't allowed inside , because when parsed as HTML, a  element's start tag will imply a  element's end tag. Thus, the following markup results in two , not one:
